🌍 Machine Translation Project

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 What is Machine Translation?

Machine Translation converts:

👉 Text from one language → another language

---

🎯 Example

```text
Input:  "Hello"
Output: "Bonjour"
```

---

🧠 Approach

Use:

👉 Seq2Seq Models
👉 Attention
👉 Transformers

---

🔄 Workflow

```text
Parallel Text Dataset
   ↓
Tokenization
   ↓
Encoder (Input Language)
   ↓
Decoder (Output Language)
   ↓
Translated Text
```

---

📊 Dataset Example

| English      | French         |
| ------------ | -------------- |
| Hello        | Bonjour        |
| How are you? | Comment ça va? |

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚙️ Basic TensorFlow Seq2Seq Example

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```python
from tensorflow import keras
from tensorflow.keras import layers

encoder = layers.LSTM(256, return_state=True)
decoder = layers.LSTM(256, return_sequences=True)

# Simplified example
encoder_outputs, state_h, state_c = encoder(encoder_input)
decoder_outputs = decoder(decoder_input, initial_state=[state_h, state_c])
```

---

🔥 Transformer-Based Translation (Modern)

---

```python
from transformers import pipeline

translator = pipeline("translation_en_to_fr")

print(translator("Hello, how are you?"))
```

---

📊 Evaluation Metrics

---

BLEU Score

Measures translation quality.

* Higher = better translation

